From 9ab3f82b90884e3011dfdea1b3df60c2944e370c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:26:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] fix: stabilize issue live comment updates

Clear the comment form's dropzone after a live submit so already submitted
attachments are not re-sent and moved to the next comment, and restore the
buttons' state for the emptied editor.

Replace changed timeline parts instead of morphing them, so rendered markup
(mermaid, code copy, task lists) is initialized again, and keep the connection
indicator out of the timeline entries, which caused entries to be re-inserted
and their markup to be initialized twice.

Publish timeline invalidations from the notifier, so changes made outside of
the web handlers (API, merges, reviews, pushes) reach live pages, and add the
missing whois module requirement.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
